---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Validation & Declarations | Governance Commons" description="Version-scoped Governance Commons validation support, evidence expectations, and declaration boundaries.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-title"><p class="eyebrow">Validation &amp; declarations</p><h1>Say exactly what was checked.</h1><p class="lede">A Governance Commons claim names one specification, one version, one subject, one validation method, and the evidence retained. The umbrella itself is not an adoption or certification target.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section white">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <h2>Current automated support</h2>
      <table class="profile-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Target</th><th>Published support</th><th>Public claim boundary</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Agent Dossier</strong></td><td>Current Python source contains structural dossier validation, with candidate-wheel CI at commit <code>5987cd9</code>. Published Python 0.2.0 does not expose the Dossier target.</td><td>Until a newer Python package is published, use the exact source commit and label the evidence source-based rather than registry-installed.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>ONS</strong></td><td>Python 0.2.0 and npm 0.1.1 expose ONS validation, but current toolkit rules identify ONS v1.4.0 while the latest ONS repo release is v1.3.0.</td><td>Do not treat the toolkit/release mismatch as proof of ONS v1.3.0 conformance.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Agent Matrix</strong></td><td>Repository source validator and tests; no shared published gc-validate target.</td><td>Label evidence manual or provisional and record the exact commit used.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>APO</strong></td><td>Runtime tests and local validation commands.</td><td>APO is a reference-runtime candidate, not a specification or conformance target.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>ATP</strong></td><td>Pre-release schema and conformance tests.</td><td>No public badge or released conformance claim.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Governance Record</strong></td><td>Python governance-commons 0.2.0.</td><td>Validation checks the record contract; it does not grant authority or certify the underlying action.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="section-inner detail-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Evidence levels</p><h2>Automated, manual, and provisional are different claims.</h2>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li><strong>Automated:</strong> a published validator explicitly supports the named target and version.</li>
          <li><strong>Manual:</strong> documented checks were performed by an identified reviewer without a supported published validator.</li>
          <li><strong>Provisional:</strong> useful implementation evidence exists, but version alignment, validator coverage, or release maturity remains unresolved.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <aside class="resource-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Declaration record</p><ol class="number-list"><li>Name the specification and exact version.</li><li>Identify the subject and validator or manual procedure.</li><li>Retain the ConformanceReport or manual evidence.</li><li>Record unsupported rules, skips, and uncertainty.</li><li>Submit an adopter entry only with those limits visible.</li></ol><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/governancecommons/governance-commons/blob/main/ADOPTERS.md">View ADOPTERS.md →</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/governancecommons/governance-commons/blob/main/docs/conformance/badge-criteria.md">Detailed criteria →</a></aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section white"><div class="section-inner notice"><strong>Certification boundary:</strong> Governance Commons does not operate a certification program. Maintainer review of a declaration is a completeness check, not independent re-validation or endorsement.</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
